## 💾 Persistence Model

**Philosophy**: *"Signal + Self-Host Flexibility"* — Client-side storage by default; server persistence is opt-in.

| Tier | Default | Controls | Purpose |
|------|---------|----------|---------|
| **Client (IndexedDB)** | ✅ Always | User | Personal history, offline access |
| **Server (STDB memory)** | ✅ Always | Server admin | Real-time sync, active sessions |
| **Server (disk files)** | ❌ Opt-in | Server admin | Compliance, audit, backup |
| **server-auditor addon** | ❌ Opt-in | Server admin | Structured archival + retention |

**Channel Persistence Modes** (per-channel config):
1. **Ephemeral** (default) — TTL 5 min, memory only
2. **Session-Only** — Survives until server restart
3. **Persistent (Disk)** — JSONL files, retention policies

**File Format**: Append-only JSONL at `~/.wabi/data/{server_id}/channels/{channel_id}/messages.jsonl`

